# Tasks: Screen-news WebSocket subscriptions

Plan: `speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.plan` (contracts in §3, algorithm in §4)
Status: T-preflight, T00-T10 and T12 completed for the authorized scope on 2026-10-09. T11, working/live database changes and deployment remain deferred. Application validation is compile-only; iOS acceptance is static-only, not Swift compilation or runtime proof.

## Execution acceptance — 2026-10-09

- The user confirmed `k8infra/mysql_8/Dump20260524.sql` as the `login_` working source and explicitly selected `mysql_8/book.sql` as the supplemental `book` baseline, acknowledging its older data. Untouched byte-for-byte copies and original implementation snapshots were preserved before edits.
- Generated the full standalone `k8infra/mysql_8/screen_news_standalone_rc.sql`. The only schema delta is signed `news_settings.logins_id INT NOT NULL` plus `UK_NEWS_SETTINGS_LOGINS_ID`; original PK/FK, unrelated schema objects and source data remain intact.
- All three prescribed Maven compile-only commands succeeded after backend edits. iOS T08-T09 received specialist static approval after correcting the socket lifecycle and reconnect cancellation; no `swiftc`, `xcodebuild`, application startup or runtime tests ran.
- Database Engineer accepted an RC-only import into fresh isolated MySQL 8.0.46, with socket-only access, no network, no host database mounts and `lower_case_table_names=1`. Comparisons preserved 21 tables / 3,561 rows, 3 views, 24 procedures and 10 triggers; all 14 declared FK relationships were orphan-free. All 18 bounded parameterized SQL acceptance checks passed. Both disposable targets were removed.
- T12 Backend Engineer approved task compliance and the final model/compile/SQL evidence. This is not a security-hardening or ORM/API runtime sign-off.

