## T04 — dalogin forwarding servlet (Backend Engineer; protected auth/session contract)

Files:
- `dalogin-quarkus/src/main/java/com/dalogin/client/service/NewsSettings.java` (new interface, like `User.java`): `@GET` and `@PUT` on `@Path("/rest/news-settings/screen")`. The PUT takes a `String` JSON body.
- `dalogin-quarkus/src/main/java/com/dalogin/client/ServiceClient.java`: add `callGetNewsScreen()` and `callPutNewsScreen(String json)`, with `logOutboundRequest`/`logOutboundResponse` as in `callGetData`.
- `dalogin-quarkus/src/main/java/com/dalogin/servlets/AdminServlet.java` (extend existing; no NewsSettingsServlet):
  - Keep `/admin` and add the exact urlPattern `/admin/newsSettings/screen`; do not map the servlet to `/admin/*`.
  - Dispatch using `getServletPath()` equal to `/admin/newsSettings/screen` with null `getPathInfo()`. Add `doPut`; keep `/admin` GET/POST behaviour and responses unchanged. POST on the news path returns 405 with `Allow: GET, PUT`.
  - Keep `processRequest`, `performTask`, their existing session/user/device/token/activation checks and exception handling unchanged. Add no token/token2/activation-null or session-identity guards. Never take identity from client inputs.
  - Keep `handleActivationRequired` unchanged on both routes: activation `"S"` calls `AdminResponses.prepareActivationRequired` and the existing account-profile `callServiceAndRespond`, returning legacy 300, `Response: S`, `X-Token` and account-profile body. No news-settings forwarding or preference mutation, including on PUT.
  - In `handleLoginForActivedUser`, retain its existing `getToken2(deviceId)` lookup/exception handling and `buildAttributes`. Add one branch choosing new `callNewsSettingsAndRespond(response, request, attributes)` on the news path versus existing `callServiceAndRespond` otherwise; keep that legacy method unchanged.
  - The new method forwards active GET/PUT to `/mbook-1/rest/news-settings/screen`, with raw PUT JSON and existing session-derived attributes/RequestFilter headers. Pass the mbook status/body through unchanged and close the downstream Response and ServiceClient.
  - iOS uses `loginPath("admin/newsSettings/screen")`.
- `dalogin-quarkus/src/main/java/com/dalogin/servlets/responsemap/AdminResponses.java`: add `newsSettingsDownstream(response, statusCode, contentType, body)`; leave legacy `downstreamBody` unchanged.
- `dalogin-quarkus/src/main/java/com/dalogin/filters/AuthFilter.java`: no edit; its existing `/admin/*` mapping already covers the new path.

Done when:
- `user` comes only from `HttpSession`.
- The headers match plan §3.2.
- A request without a session is stopped by the existing AuthFilter (current no-session response: 502). News requests requiring activation return the existing 300 activation headers/account-profile body with no settings call or mutation. That body is not `ScreenNews`; iOS uses existing activation response handling. Active news requests pass all mbook statuses/bodies through unchanged, including unrelated filter 403. Existing `/admin` GET/POST responses remain unchanged.

