## Dependencies

T-preflight snapshots precede each file's first change in T00–T09; recording the user-confirmed dump/checksum and preserving its untouched copy precede T01 RC generation. T00 is the prerequisite for all mbook tasks.
- T02, T03, T05 and T06 start after T00 has been reviewed.
- T01 starts after its T-preflight source/copy prerequisite, but is independent of T00. T04, T08 and T09 are independent of T00 and of each other (no file overlap).
- T06 after T02 and T05.
- T07 after T06.
- T09 can be written in parallel (the contract is fixed); its review waits for T04.
- T10 after T00–T09: RC generation → static matching against final T02/T07 models/DAO writes → isolated full import/insertion validation. All SQL execution waits until edits are complete.
- T12 after final edits, successful T10 compiles and Database Engineer's SQL acceptance evidence; fixes loop through RC regeneration/static matching/fresh-target retest when impacted.
- T11 after T10, T12 approval and separate runtime approval.
